# Deise stage PT1: Hadur as the teacher for Deise's bullet power (thread "Pack more strategy per
# byte in codesize bots"). Sanaro's n06 (PR #514) passed the same idea at nano size: Hadur's power
# decisions, recorded at every shot and packed into a string, HS +0.55 +- 0.31 over 0.2. A string
# costs Deise only its charAt read (codesize counts method bytes, not the constant pool), so the
# table arm is 1,488 B by javac against 0.4's 1,475: 13 of Deise's free bytes, the rest stays free
# for the Deise thread's per-opponent aim rows.
# pc-deise-e07/e08 found 0.4's curve log10(energy) x 325 / distance at a peak for a one-line
# formula (240 read -0.37, 500 -0.42, 900 -1.15). A table is not one curve: it can be harder close
# and in the endgame and softer where Hadur is, cell by cell, so this asks a different question.
#   ./queue.sh run pc-deise-pt1        (or  .\queue.ps1 run pc-deise-pt1)
# Run it from master:
#   git checkout master && git pull
# One bench queue, RoboRumble workers at 0, unpinned, 12 workers. A rerun skips every seat that
# finished; a seat stopped part-way is fought again from its start (the melee path has no per-battle
# resume). No step needs a decision. Nothing here touches Hadur, Saor or the shipped Deise class.
#
# Steps:
#   teach  Hadur 3.20 (the released jar, fetched into opponents/ as any opponent) in Deise's seat on the live-shaped census: 46 fields x 6 seeds (base 5100) =
#          276 battles, about 20 min. Its only product is work/deise-pt1/live-TEACH/*/battles/*/
#          shots.csv (BENCH-155: own energy, distance and power at every shot).
#   build  tools/deise_power.py writes two flat classes on 0.4's shipped Deise.java, the power line
#          read from POWER.charAt((energy << 7) + distance / 16) in fortieths (511 energy rows), each printing how many
#          of its 65,408 cells came from Hadur:
#            PTS  2 x 2 blocks (2 energy x 32 px) with 20+ shots (Sanaro's HS shape)
#            PTB  4 x 4 blocks with 10+ shots (wider reach, coarser)
#          Every other cell keeps 0.4's formula averaged over the cell, so an arm differs from D
#          only where Hadur's shots agree, plus the table's rounding (16 px, fortieths):
#            PT0  the table with no Hadur cells at all, the rounding alone (a control for it)
#          Then tools/deise_arms.sh builds D, PT0, PTS and PTB.
#   D, PT0, PTS, PTB  the live-shaped census, 46 fields x 6 fresh seeds (base 5200) = 276 battles a
#          seat, about 17 min each.
# About 1.6 h in all on the PC.
# Read against D, field by field (PT0 should read level; if it does not, read PTS and PTB against
# PT0 too). An arm passes when its gain's low end is above 0 (Deise's +0.30
# bar is for a ship; a pass here first goes to the Deise thread, which fits it beside its rows).
# Caveat (as n06): the teach run and the bench share the census fields, on different seeds.
# Stop rules on every census step (docs/bench/watch.md; halt, finished seats are kept, the stopped
# seat reruns from its start): 20 failed battles (a broken jar), no battle in 30 minutes (a hung
# step), or 40+ skipped turns a battle over the last 100 (the PR #331 build-up). A halt at worst
# leaves the rest of that seat and the seats after it unrun, at most 1,380 battles (about 1.6 h).
# No early finish on score: a census seat is one robot. ALERT opens an issue for Leigh on a stop.

set MVN = mvn -q -Drobocode.version=1.11.1 compile exec:java
set OUT = ../docs/bench/local
set ALERT = lgriffin
set ARMS = D,PT0,PTS,PTB

prep | (cd .. && mvn -q -DskipTests install -pl deise -am) && curl -fsSLo opponents/hadur117.Hadur_3.20.jar https://github.com/lgriffin/Hadur_Robot/releases/download/v3.20/hadur117.Hadur_3.20.jar && cp ../deise/target/hadur117.mini.Deise_0.4.jar opponents/ && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set minimelee-field.txt && for f in melee-census-317/f*.txt; do ./fetch-opponents.sh --set "$f" || exit 1; done && DEISE_RUN=pt1 bash tools/deise_arms.sh live 6 5100 TEACH

live-TEACH | ${MVN} "-Dexec.args=@work/deise-pt1/live-TEACH.args"
  after: prep
  watch: battles=276
  stop: fails 20
  stop: stall 30m
  stop: skips 40 over 100

build | python3 tools/deise_power.py 'work/deise-pt1/live-TEACH/*/battles/*/shots.csv' --own-step 2 --dist-step 2 --min 20 --out work/deise-pt1/PTS.java && python3 tools/deise_power.py 'work/deise-pt1/live-TEACH/*/battles/*/shots.csv' --own-step 4 --dist-step 4 --min 10 --out work/deise-pt1/PTB.java && python3 tools/deise_power.py 'work/deise-pt1/live-TEACH/*/battles/*/shots.csv' --min 1000000000 --out work/deise-pt1/PT0.java && DEISE_RUN=pt1 bash tools/deise_arms.sh live 6 5200 ${ARMS} && python3 tools/kitlab_codesize.py work/deise-pt1/hadur117.mini.DeisePTS_0.4.jar | tail -1 && python3 tools/kitlab_codesize.py work/deise-pt1/hadur117.mini.DeisePTB_0.4.jar | tail -1
  after: live-TEACH

live-D | ${MVN} "-Dexec.args=@work/deise-pt1/live-D.args"
  after: build
  watch: battles=276
  stop: fails 20
  stop: stall 30m
  stop: skips 40 over 100

live-PT0 | ${MVN} "-Dexec.args=@work/deise-pt1/live-PT0.args"
  after: live-D
  watch: battles=276
  stop: fails 20
  stop: stall 30m
  stop: skips 40 over 100

live-PTS | ${MVN} "-Dexec.args=@work/deise-pt1/live-PTS.args"
  after: live-PT0
  watch: battles=276
  stop: fails 20
  stop: stall 30m
  stop: skips 40 over 100

live-PTB | ${MVN} "-Dexec.args=@work/deise-pt1/live-PTB.args"
  after: live-PTS
  watch: battles=276
  stop: fails 20
  stop: stall 30m
  stop: skips 40 over 100

read | python3 tools/saor_arms.py --work-root work/deise-pt1 --field live --arms ${ARMS} --control D --only work/deise-pt1/live/micro.txt --pairings 203 --robot-prefix hadur117.mini.Deise --arms-file deise-arms/arms.txt > ${OUT}/deise-pt1-vs-d.md
  after: live-PTB

pr | bash tools/open_results_pr.sh claude/pc-deise-pt1-results "Deise stage PT1: Hadur's power table" ${OUT}/deise-pt1-vs-d.md ${OUT}/deise-pt1-live-*.md
  after: read
